267	    // read-only / WARL-illegal CSR raises cmderr in the Program Buffer, and a
268	    // batched sweep cannot tolerate a mid-batch fault the way the abstract path's
269	    // per-CSR clear_cmderr does. Restoring those CSRs is a no-op anyway (can't
270	    // write a read-only CSR), so restore keeps the abstract-tolerant path until a
271	    // per-CSR writability model can gate the sweep. The DRAIN sweep IS on (csrr
272	    // reads never fault for a readable CSR) -- see set_block_store_drain.
